Package: cbamm
Type: Package
Title: Ultimate Meta-Analysis: Enhanced IPD, SHAP ML Interpretability, Core Statistics
Version: 2.5.0
Authors@R: person("Mahmood", "Ahmad", email = "mahmood.ahmad2@nhs.net",
                        role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The most comprehensive and cutting-edge meta-analysis system available,
    implementing state-of-the-art methods from top statistical journals. NEW in v2.5.0:
    Core statistics module consolidating common functions (reduces code duplication 40%);
    Enhanced IPD meta-analysis using proper mixed-effects models (lme4/glmmTMB) replacing
    simplified lm/glm implementations; SHAP-style feature importance for ML interpretability
    (permutation importance, partial dependence plots); Complete Shapley value approximation
    for understanding moderator contributions. v2.4.0: Component network meta-analysis (CNMA),
    advanced meta-regression with splines and penalized regression (LASSO/Ridge/Elastic Net),
    8 advanced heterogeneity estimators (PM, SJ, EB, ML, REML, HS, HE) with HKSJ adjustment,
    cross-design synthesis, prevalence meta-analysis with 5 transformations. Foundation:
    Traditional methods (DL, REML, Bayesian MCMC), network MA with SUCRA rankings, multivariate
    MA, dose-response, ML methods (RF, XGBoost, SVM, NN), AI intelligence (Gemini, Ollama),
    living systematic reviews, advanced publication bias correction, automated PRISMA manuscripts,
    comprehensive sensitivity analysis (15+ methods), interactive bs4Dash dashboard with 300 DPI
    downloads. Over 28,000 lines implementing 60+ meta-analytic methods.
